  "metadata": {
    "id": "typical-deck-detail",
    "title": "Typical Deck Post-to-Footing & Beam Framing Detail",
    "description": "Typical deck post-to-footing foundation, ABU standoff post base, notched double 2x8 beam, LUS joist hanger, 2x10 deck joist, and 2x6 decking assembly.",
    "category": "Structural Framing",
    "tags": [
      "deck",
      "foundation",
      "footing",
      "wood",
      "framing",
      "rebar",
      "residential"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Origin (0, 0) is at the post/plinth/footing centerline on the top surface of the concrete plinth.",
      "Monolithic concrete pier and spread footing with vertical plinth bars, horizontal ties, bottom longitudinal bar, and transverse footing rebar.",
      "ABU standoff post base provides 1\" clearance above concrete plinth over embedded anchor bolt and square washer.",
      "Double 2x8 beam cross-section at post/beam intersection carries 2x10 deck joist via LUS face-mount joist hanger and 2x6 decking with 1/4\" drainage gaps."
    ]
  },
